---
/**
 * Terms of use.
 *
 * Ported from the old Next.js app and CORRECTED. The old terms described a
 * product that "is not a dispatch system, ELD, GPS product, load board, or
 * invoicing system" and promised nothing about loads or pay. Dispatch, loads,
 * customers, settlements and IFTA all ship now, so §"What the service does"
 * names them. The old fee section priced by fleet-size BANDS; this product
 * prices per power unit with a monthly minimum, so that section was rewritten
 * rather than ported.
 *
 * Also dropped, because no such feature exists in this repository: driver
 * update links, document upload, customer self-serve export, and user
 * administration by the owner. Searched for, not assumed.
 *
 * The limitation section matters more than usual here: a deadline tracker that
 * is mistaken for a guarantee of compliance is a liability, so the page says
 * outright what the product is not. Draft, unreviewed — see the notice at the
 * foot.
 */
import Public from '../layouts/Public.astro'
import {
  CONTACT_EMAIL,
  EFFECTIVE_DATE,
  JURISDICTION,
  LEGAL_ENTITY,
  PRODUCT_NAME,
  SITE_HOST,
  SITE_URL,
  VENUE,
} from '../lib/legal.ts'
import { site } from '../lib/site.ts'

const h2 = 'text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight'
const p = 'mt-2 text-sm text-ink-500'
const list = 'mt-2 space-y-2 text-sm text-ink-500'
// `.link` from global.css: underlined at rest, not only under the cursor.
// A link that is nothing but a different blue is a link a reader in a hurry
// does not see, and half this audience is reading a second language.
const link = 'link'
---

<Public title="Terms" description="The terms of using FleetView Compliance.">
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-14 sm:px-6">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">Terms</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-500">Effective {EFFECTIVE_DATE}</p>

    <div class="mt-8 space-y-6 text-ink-700">
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-amber-300 bg-amber-50 p-5">
        <h2 class={`${h2} text-amber-900`}>What this service is not</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-amber-900">
          We keep records and send reminders. <strong>We are not a law firm, we do not give legal
          advice, and we do not file anything with any agency for you.</strong> Using this service
          does not make you compliant, and nothing here says that you are. Meeting every rule that
          applies to your business stays your job.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class={h2}>Who this is between</h2>
        <p class={p}>
          This agreement is between {LEGAL_ENTITY} (&ldquo;we&rdquo;, &ldquo;us&rdquo;) and the
          carrier that opens the account (&ldquo;you&rdquo;). Your staff use the service under
          your account and with your permission. If you accept for a company, you are saying you
          are allowed to bind it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class={h2}>What the service does</h2>
        <p class={p}>{PRODUCT_NAME} is software for small trucking carriers. It can:</p>
        <ul class={list}>
          <li>
            track federal and California deadlines for your drivers and trucks, and show the
            regulation each one comes from so you can check our work;
          </li>
          <li>show what is overdue, due soon, or on track — worst first;</li>
          <li>hold your loads, stops, customers and brokers, and dispatch a driver to a load;</li>
          <li>warn you, or stop you, when the driver or truck you picked is not qualified;</li>
          <li>work out driver pay and produce settlements;</li>
          <li>add up fuel and miles by state and prepare your IFTA figures;</li>
          <li>
            make a <strong>proof link</strong> so a broker, an insurer or a shipper you choose can
            see a summary without signing in;
          </li>
          <li>send the email digest and alerts you set up;</li>
          <li>offer a free public USDOT check against public federal data, with no account.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class={p}>
          Current prices are on the <a class={link} href="/pricing">pricing page</a>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class={h2}>What it does not do</h2>
        <p class={p}>
          We do not file your MCS-150, UCR, IFTA return, Clean Truck Check report, medical
          certificate, or anything else. You file those yourself, in the agency's own system. We
          tell you when something is due.
        </p>
        <p class={p}>
          We are not an ELD. We do not log hours of service and we do not track trucks by GPS. We
          do not run payroll and we do not send invoices to your brokers for you. We are not your
          lawyer, your accountant, or your safety director, and using {PRODUCT_NAME} does not make
          us any of those.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class={h2}>Accuracy, and its limits</h2>
        <p class={p}>
          We take care with the rules we encode and we show the citation so you can check them.
          Rules change, agencies publish corrections, and public data is sometimes wrong or out of
          date. Where we are not sure, we say so instead of guessing.
        </p>
        <p class={p}>
          Two limits are plain. First, a calculated date can still be wrong — a rule changed, a
          source was misread, or the software failed. Second, every figure depends on what you
          typed: a wrong medical expiry, a wrong truck weight or a wrong odometer gives a
          confident wrong answer. IFTA figures and settlement figures are arithmetic on your
          numbers, not an audited return or a payroll filing.
        </p>
        <p class={p}>
          <strong>
            Treat {PRODUCT_NAME} as a well-informed assistant, not as the legal record of whether
            you are compliant or of what you owe.
          </strong> Where it matters, check it against the source and the agency.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class={h2}>Your account</h2>
        <p class={p}>
          You are responsible for everything done under your logins and for what is typed in. Keep
          passwords private. Do not share them. Tell us quickly if you think someone has got into
          an account.
        </p>
        <p class={p}>
          Accounts are for your own fleet. You may not resell access without our agreement.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class={h2}>Your data and your drivers</h2>
        <p class={p}>
          Your records stay yours. We use them to run the service for you and for nothing else. We
          do not sell them and we do not use them to train machine-learning models. See the
          <a class={link} href="/privacy"> privacy policy</a>, which is part of these terms.
        </p>
        <p class={p}>
          You will enter personal information about your drivers. You confirm you are allowed to
          give it to us and to tell us to process it, and that you have given your drivers any
          notice the law requires. For driver records we act as your service provider.
        </p>
        <p class={p}>
          Ask us for a copy of your data at any time and we will send it. After the agreement ends
          we hold the data for a short period so you can still ask, then delete it as the privacy
          policy describes.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class={h2}>Proof links</h2>
        <p class={p}>
          A proof link lets whoever holds it see a summary you chose, without signing in. That is
          what it is for. You choose what it covers, how long it lasts and who you send it to, and
          you can revoke it. Until then, anyone who has the link — including anyone it was
          forwarded to — can open it. Treat it like a password.
        </p>
        <p class={p}>
          A proof page is a dated summary of what is in your account. It is not a certificate from
          us that you are compliant.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class={h2}>The free USDOT check</h2>
        <p class={p}>
          The free check on our website reads public federal data. It does not create an account
          and it is not a guarantee of accuracy. The federal record can be incomplete or out of
          date, and the source is sometimes slow or unavailable.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class={h2}>Payment</h2>
        <p class={p}>
          Billed monthly in advance at the published rate, based on the number of power units on
          your account, with a monthly minimum. There is no contract and no minimum term — cancel
          whenever you like and you will not be billed again. We do not refund part-months, but we
          will not bill you for a month you did not use. Prices exclude any tax that applies.
        </p>
        <p class={p}>
          If your truck count changes, the rate follows it from the next billing period. We will
          not stop tracking your deadlines just because the count moved.
        </p>
        <p class={p}>
          We will give at least 30 days' notice by email before changing the price of an existing
          subscription. If a payment fails we will try to reach you before switching off paid
          features, and we will not delete your data for non-payment without telling you first.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class={h2}>Availability</h2>
        <p class={p}>
          We try to keep the service running, but we do not promise it will never be down and we
          do not offer an uptime guarantee. Alerts travel over email and phone networks we do not
          control. An alert that did not arrive is not proof that a deadline did not exist. The
          service is provided as is, apart from warranties the law does not let us exclude.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class={h2}>Acceptable use</h2>
        <p class={p}>
          Use {PRODUCT_NAME} for your own fleet, lawfully. Do not try to reach another carrier's
          data, attack or interfere with the service, abuse the free USDOT check, scrape the
          service, or resell it without our agreement. Do not use a proof link to harass anyone or
          to disclose personal information unlawfully. We may suspend an account being used to
          harm others or the service, and we will say why when we reasonably can.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class={h2}>Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p class={p}>
          To the fullest extent the law allows, neither side is liable for indirect, incidental or
          consequential losses, or for lost profits or lost business, arising from this agreement.
        </p>
        <p class={p}>
          To the fullest extent the law allows, our total liability for any claim arising out of
          or relating to {PRODUCT_NAME} is limited to the fees you paid us in the twelve months
          before the event that gave rise to the claim, or one hundred US dollars if you have paid
          us nothing.
        </p>
        <p class={p}>
          Nothing here limits liability for fraud, for death or personal injury caused by
          negligence, or for anything else that cannot lawfully be limited. Because wrong or
          missing compliance information can put a truck out of service, you agree that this
          product's role is help and organisation — not a guarantee against that happening.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class={h2}>Ending the agreement</h2>
        <p class={p}>
          You can stop using {PRODUCT_NAME} and cancel at any time. We may end this agreement on
          30 days' notice, or sooner for a serious or repeated breach of these terms. After it
          ends, we keep and delete data as the privacy policy describes.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class={h2}>Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p class={p}>
          We may update these terms. If a change materially affects your rights we will email
          account holders at least 30 days beforehand where we can, and using the service after
          the change takes effect means you accept it. If you do not accept it, you may cancel. If
          you had prepaid for a period you no longer want only because of that change, we will
          refund the unused part.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class={h2}>Governing law</h2>
        <p class={p}>
          These terms are governed by the laws of {JURISDICTION}, without regard to its
          conflict-of-laws rules. The courts of {VENUE} have exclusive jurisdiction, and both
          sides agree to that.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class={h2}>Contact</h2>
        <p class={p}>
          {LEGAL_ENTITY}
        </p>
        <p class={p}>
          <a class={link} href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a><br />
          <a class={link} href={SITE_URL}>{SITE_HOST}</a>
        </p>
        {/* The only place the business address appears. It is kept off the
            marketing pages deliberately, but a terms and a privacy page are
            expected to name where the business is, and a payment processor
            will ask for it. */}
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink-500">{site.legalLocation}</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <p class={p}>
          See also our <a class={link} href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> and
          <a class={link} href="/pricing"> pricing</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-10 rounded-lg bg-amber-50 px-4 py-3 text-sm text-amber-900">
      <strong>Draft.</strong> These terms have not yet been reviewed by a lawyer. That must be
      done before launch.
    </p>
  </section>
</Public>
